---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Oscar's Classic Model Cars Collection">
  <section class="about-section">
    <h2 class="about-title">About the Collection</h2>

    <div class="about-content">
      <p class="lead">
        Oscar's Classic Model Cars Collection represents over 30 years of passionate collecting,
        featuring more than 700 vintage automotive miniatures from the pre-1960 era.
      </p>

      <h3>The Collector</h3>
      <p>
        Oscar Alvarado began collecting classic model cars in 1994, drawn to the craftsmanship
        and historical significance of vintage automotive miniatures. What started as a small
        hobby has grown into one of the most comprehensive collections of pre-war and early
        post-war model vehicles.
      </p>

      <h3>The Collection</h3>
      <p>
        The collection spans vehicles from 1862 to the 1960s, featuring models from renowned
        manufacturers including Matchbox, Dinky, Corgi, Franklin Mint, Brooklin Models, and many others.
        Each piece is carefully catalogued with details about the original vehicle, the model manufacturer,
        scale, materials, and production information.
      </p>

      <h3>Featured Categories</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Touring Cars</strong> - Classic automobiles for everyday travel</li>
        <li><strong>Racing Cars</strong> - Vintage motorsport legends</li>
        <li><strong>Commercial Vehicles</strong> - Trucks, vans, and delivery vehicles</li>
        <li><strong>Buses & Coaches</strong> - Public transportation through the ages</li>
        <li><strong>Emergency Vehicles</strong> - Fire engines, ambulances, and police cars</li>
        <li><strong>Steam & Locomotives</strong> - Early mechanical transportation</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Scales & Materials</h3>
      <p>
        The majority of models are in 1:43 scale, the most popular size for collectible diecast vehicles.
        The collection includes pieces made from diecast metal, white metal, plastic, and resin,
        representing the evolution of model-making techniques over decades.
      </p>

      <h3>This Website</h3>
      <p>
        This digital catalogue was created to share the collection with fellow enthusiasts worldwide.
        Originally maintained as a blog, the collection has been migrated to this modern platform
        for easier browsing, searching, and filtering.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-section {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .about-content {
    background: var(--card-background);
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-color);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }

  li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  li strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .about-content {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
